RAWM.CONF(5)

# NAME

rawm.conf - rawm window-manager configuration

# DESCRIPTION

*rawm.conf* configures only state owned by *rawm*(1): managed-client borders,
client geometry policy, layouts, tags, rules, and pointer operations that
directly manipulate admitted clients.

Global keyboard bindings, argv execution, persistent or transient desktop
presentation, status collection, ALSA state, and system-tray ownership are not
part of this schema. In a rawmkit desktop those authorities belong to separate
components. Extracted settings fail validation instead of being accepted as
inert compatibility data.

The file uses libconfig syntax. Unknown settings, wrong types, invalid enum
values, out-of-range values, duplicate pointer bindings, and references to
nonexistent tags are rejected.

# FILES AND PRECEDENCE

Without *-c*, rawm starts with built-in defaults and then applies these layers:

. _/etc/rawm/rawm.conf_
. _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rawm/rawm.conf_ when *XDG_CONFIG_HOME* is an absolute path,
  otherwise _$HOME/.config/rawm/rawm.conf_

Missing normal system/user files are ignored. Existing files must be regular
files and must parse and validate successfully.

With *rawm -c PATH*, built-in defaults are followed by exactly _PATH_; the
normal system and user files are bypassed.

Use *rawm -C* to validate the effective configuration without opening X.

# LAYERING

Scalar and grouped settings override only members present in a later layer.
The following lists replace the corresponding earlier list when present:

*tags.default*
	The complete default tag list.

*tags.monitors*
	The complete per-monitor tag override list.

*rules*
	The complete rule list.

*pointer.bindings*
	The complete admitted-client pointer binding list.

# VALUE REFERENCES

The string values under *ui.colors* support *${path}* references after all
layers have been read. References may point to another color or to these scalar
paths:

- *ui.border_width*
- *ui.snap*
- *ui.opacity*
- *behavior.dialog_center*
- *behavior.size_hints*
- *behavior.floating_placement*
- *behavior.cascade_step*
- *layout.master_factor*
- *layout.master_count*
- *layout.gaps.inner*
- *layout.gaps.outer*
- *layout.gaps.smart*

References are recursive. Cycles, unknown paths, empty references, and
unterminated references are errors. Write *$${path}* to preserve the literal
text *${path}*.

# UI

The *ui* group accepts *border_width*, *snap*, *opacity*, and *colors*.

*border_width* = _integer_
	Managed-client border width in pixels, from 0 through 64. Default: 2.

*snap* = _integer_
	Pointer move/resize snap threshold in pixels, from 0 through 4096. Default:
	32.

*opacity* = _number_
	Client opacity projection from 0.0 through 1.0. Default: 1.0.

## Colors

*ui.colors* accepts four border-color strings:

*normal*
	Unselected managed client. Default: *#cccccc*.

*selected*
	Selected tiled client. Default: *#0066ff*.

*urgent*
	Client with admitted urgency. Default: *#0066ff*.

*floating*
	Selected elevated/floating client. Default: *${ui.colors.selected}*.

Font, foreground/background, and OSD settings are presentation policy and are
not accepted by rawm.

# BEHAVIOR

The *behavior* group accepts client-geometry policy.

*dialog_center* = *"none"* | *"monitor"* | *"parent"*
	Default centering policy for eligible floating/dialog clients. Default: none.
	Rules may override this per match.

*size_hints* = *"never"* | *"floating"* | *"always"*
	When ICCCM size hints constrain client geometry. Default: floating.

*floating_placement* = *"client"* | *"cascade"*
	Initial free-window placement policy. *client* preserves client-requested
	placement where possible; *cascade* uses rawm's monitor-local cascading
	placement. Default: cascade.

*cascade_step* = _integer_
	Cascade displacement in pixels, from 1 through 4096. Default: 32.

# LAYOUT

The *layout* group controls the tiled geometry model.

*master_factor* = _number_
	Master-area fraction, from 0.05 through 0.95. Default: 0.55.

*master_count* = _integer_
	Number of master clients, from 0 through 64. Default: 1.

## Gaps

*layout.gaps* accepts:

*inner* = _integer_
	Gap between tiled clients, from 0 through 4096. Default: 0.

*outer* = _integer_
	Gap between tiled clients and the monitor work-area edge, from 0 through 4096.
	Default: 0.

*smart* = _boolean_
	Suppress the outer gap when only one tiled client is present. Default: false.

Layout display symbols are presentation policy and are not accepted by rawm.
Canonical layout names are published by rawm's state membrane.

# TAGS

The *tags* group accepts *default* and *monitors*.

*tags.default* is a list containing between 1 and 31 groups. Every entry
requires:

*name* = _string_
	Tag name, at most 22 bytes.

*layout* = _layout-name_
	Initial layout for the tag. Optional; default: tile.

Valid layout names are *tile*, *floating*, *monocle*, *bstack*,
*bstack_horizontal*, and *grid*.

Per-monitor overrides in *tags.monitors* contain *monitor* and a complete *tags*
list with the same number of entries as *tags.default*.

# RULES

*rules* is a list of match groups. Match fields are *class*, *instance*,
*title*, and *role*. Policy fields are *tags*, *floating*, *center*,
*fullscreen*, *attention*, and *monitor*. Unspecified match fields are
wildcards; unspecified policy fields leave the corresponding default/admitted
state unchanged.

# POINTER

*pointer.bindings* is the complete list of rawm-owned client pointer bindings.
Each entry accepts:

*modifiers* = (_strings_)
	Optional list using *Shift*, *Control*, and *Mod1* through *Mod5*.

*button* = _integer_
	X button number, from 1 through 255.

*action* = *"move"* | *"toggle_floating"* | *"resize"*
	The admitted-client geometry operation.

The stock bindings are Mod4-Button1 move, Mod4-Button2 floating toggle, and
Mod4-Button3 resize.

# REMOVED AUTHORITY

The following historical roots/settings are rejected: *status*, *commands*,
*input*, *ui.bar*, *ui.systray*, *ui.font*, *ui.osd*, and *layout.symbols*.
They belong to other components rather than compatibility state in rawm.

# SEE ALSO

*rawm*(1)
